A catalog of popular films is being converted into stereo 3D for Meta VR Glasses ahead of the device's spring 2027 launch, under a new technology partnership between Meta and DNEG , the visual effects and animation company whose slate includes &#8220; Ramayana: Rise of a Legend .&#8221;

DNEG's Stereo team has already begun work on several of the titles. Among them is &#8220;The Hunger Games : Sunrise on the Reaping,&#8221; which Variety reported earlier this month is being converted to 3D by Meta and Lionsgate with DNEG and director Francis Lawrence. The film opens in 3D in theaters on Nov. 20 and will be available on Meta VR Glasses after its theatrical run. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories 'Woman Unknown' Breakout Mathilde Arcel on Her Venice Award-Winning Performance and Life After Her Lido Triumph: 'Everything Is Open' Benjamín Vicuña, Star of Netflix Hit Series 'Envious,' Joins ‘My Last Stand' by Goya-Winner Matías Bize

The glasses are built around a 5K micro-OLED screen, branded the Infinite Display, with 37 pixels per degree. According to DNEG, that level of sharpness lets its team produce 3D versions with theatrical-quality clarity. In some cases, the team will also step outside conventional film framing to build new immersive moments.

DNEG Global CEO Namit Malhotra said, &#8220;I'm excited and enthused to announce DNEG's partnership with Meta to deliver never-before-seen 3D content for Meta VR Glasses. The launch of Meta VR Glasses is set to be a game-changer and will give cinema fans a new way to experience their favorite movies in stunning 3D. The creative possibilities opened up by this new technology align perfectly with DNEG's stated ambition to &#8216;Transform the Future of Storytelling,' and we look forward to exploring further opportunities with the Meta team to deliver the highest-quality immersive experiences for this exciting new technology.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

DNEG has worked in stereo conversion for more than 15 years and was the first to turn a full-length Hollywood feature into stereo 3D. Its 3D work has since won multiple awards, including for Alfonso Cuar&#xF3;n's &#8220;Gravity&#8221; and Christopher McQuarrie's &#8220;Mission: Impossible &#x2013; Fallout.&#8221; More recent conversions include &#8220;Spider-Man: Brand New Day,&#8221; &#8220;Supergirl&#8221; and the live-action &#8220;How to Train Your Dragon.&#8221;

With close to three decades in the business and studios in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia, DNEG has won eight visual effects Oscars since 2011, along with BAFTA, Primetime Emmy and Visual Effects Society honors.

The Meta deal comes during a crowded stretch for the company. Its projects include &#8220;Ramayana: Rise of a Legend,&#8221; &#8220;Blade Runner 2099,&#8221; &#8220;The Cat in the Hat&#8221; and Season 3 of &#8220;The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power,&#8221; with &#8220;Dune: Part Three&#8221; and &#8220;The Angry Birds Movie 3&#8221; following in December.

EXCLUSIVE: A daughter's quest to understand her father leads to surprising revelations in the Oscar-contending documentary Ba's Book , directed by Ashley Da-L&#xEA; Duong .

We have your exclusive first look at the film in the trailer above.

For Duong, the project began with a decision to travel to Vietnam &#x2013; against her parents' wishes &#x2013; to visit the place where her father had grown up and to reconnect with his estranged family, the family he had left behind when he settled in Canada. While there, her father, Anh Duong, sent her a draft of a memoir he was writing that contained stories Ashley had never heard while growing up. She had no idea, for instance, that her father had made it to Iran in 1979 as a young college student, only to be plunged into the Islamic Revolution. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

But Ashley felt there was something missing from the pages of her father's book &#x2013; namely, insight into Anh's siblings and his mother. To help her father and her relatives process all they had gone through, Duong made the bold creative decision to cast actors in scenes reenacting key moments in their lives, like an incident in which a young Anh was nearly killed by a sniper while collecting duck eggs in a rice paddy. She filmed those scenes but also filmed the reactions of her father, grandmother, aunts and uncles witnessing those memories brought startlingly to life. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Ba's Book , produced by Oscar nominee Ina Fichman ( Fire of Love ), "offers a disarming look at the intergenerational legacy of war," according to a synopsis. The documentary premiered at the Toronto International Film Festival in September and has gone on to screen at the BFI London Film Festival, the Windsor International Film Festival, and the Montreal International Documentary Festival, among others. (It will also screen on November 24 as part of Deadline's For the Love of Docs virtual series on November 24. You can RSVP for that here ).

In a director's statement, Duong describes her father's memoir as unique. "[I]t's rare to have first-hand experience of both these Cold War conflicts [Vietnam and Iran]. Furthermore, writing about the Vietnam War directly from people like my father is uncommon in English literature. Overwhelmingly, the Vietnam War is told by either non-Vietnamese writers or Vietnamese diasporic writers too young to remember the war. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

" Ba's Book explores the legacy of forced displacement and civil war for community and familial bonds. During the Vietnam War, Da-L&#xEA; village [which gives Ashley her middle name] was the site of intense fighting, sandwiched as it was between a US Army base and a Viet Cong stronghold. With Ba and his relatives on different ideological sides, this war continues to divide my family. By following my father, my grandmother, and myself, I aim to concretely portray how trauma takes root and how it passes through generations."

Duong continues, "Our film also questions storytelling's role in healing. At the same time that I am representing my dad in my film, he's also representing me in his book. The film is transparent about the potential for connection as well as the pitfalls that arise from these two acts of reciprocal storytelling. Furthermore, we explore the communal aspect of reckoning with history as we invite my extended family and the community of Da-L&#xEA; village to participate in the storytelling."

Watch the trailer for Ba's Book above.

